public access, required
for them to do their job.

00:25:36.060 --> 00:25:41.150
And also, we want to make sure
that the GCP identity access

00:25:41.150 --> 00:25:43.400
management roles and
privileges are assigned

00:25:43.400 --> 00:25:45.897
to the groups, not individual.

00:25:45.897 --> 00:25:48.230
And then we manage these
groups and the group membership

00:25:48.230 --> 00:25:50.240
within our Alta
Active Directory.

00:25:50.240 --> 00:25:54.390
And we push these groups to
GCP via Google Cloud Directory

00:25:54.390 --> 00:25:55.910
Sync.

00:25:55.910 --> 00:25:58.658
So yeah, first you can see here
the ingest the store layer.

00:25:58.658 --> 00:26:00.200
Then this is the
layers where we have

00:26:00.200 --> 00:26:04.160
both platforms are running on
this layer, on the Google Cloud

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:07.640
Compute Engine, listening
to the real-time event

00:26:07.640 --> 00:26:12.380
from the external systems,
such as the Facebook Messenger,

00:26:12.380 --> 00:26:16.040
as the web hook, as you've seen
earlier in the Beautybot video.

00:26:16.040 --> 00:26:19.430
And then that web hook is
hosting on the cloud network

00:26:19.430 --> 00:26:21.680
services sending
the event directly

00:26:21.680 --> 00:26:24.170
to the conversation platform.

00:26:24.170 --> 00:26:26.210
And on the left-hand
side, we also

00:26:26.210 --> 00:26:30.800
see the [INAUDIBLE] system can
send the data via data stream

00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:34.375
or batch into our platform
via the Cloud Pub/Sub.

00:26:34.375 --> 00:26:35.750
Within the
conversation platform,

00:26:35.750 --> 00:26:38.390
we have a interplay
component, which

00:26:38.390 --> 00:26:40.970
is orchestrate all the
incoming and outgoing traffics

00:26:40.970 --> 00:26:45.080
in the front, and also
communicate with our NLP engine

00:26:45.080 --> 00:26:48.680
for the message intent
or intent message--

00:26:48.680 --> 00:26:52.320
for example, the missing reward
points that we saw earlier.

00:26:52.320 --> 00:26:54.830
And then also,
interacting with what

00:26:54.830 --> 00:26:58.310
we call it the quasi running
inside the personalization

00:26:58.310 --> 00:26:59.600
engine.

00:26:59.600 --> 00:27:03.020
This is the place where we
have a complete 360 data

00:27:03.020 --> 00:27:07.967
view of our guests with
real-time intelligent models.

00:27:07.967 --> 00:27:10.550
And then also, it's playing the
key role in the Virtual Beauty

00:27:10.550 --> 00:27:13.230
Advisor that we saw earlier.

00:27:13.230 --> 00:27:17.570
So now, we have the data coming
from the batch, data streaming,

00:27:17.570 --> 00:27:21.170
real-time event, real-time
data integration flowing

00:27:21.170 --> 00:27:22.520
into that ingest and store.

00:27:22.520 --> 00:27:24.810
How do we store all this data?

00:27:24.810 --> 00:27:27.320
So the answer, we use
the cloud storage,

00:27:27.320 --> 00:27:29.762
what we specify as
unstructured raw data.

00:27:29.762 --> 00:27:31.220
And then the
important thing is, we

00:27:31.220 --> 00:27:33.453
want both platform
be able to use

00:27:33.453 --> 00:27:35.120
and read the data
from the cloud storage

00:27:35.120 --> 00:27:37.400
for our continuous
machine learning,

00:27:37.400 --> 00:27:39.830
machine training,
models training,

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:42.140
is a switching point for us.

00:27:42.140 --> 00:27:46.520
And now next layer, we have
the process and transformation,

00:27:46.520 --> 00:27:50.150
which we use the Cloud
Dataflow to process and enrich

00:27:50.150 --> 00:27:55.010
the data into our BigQuery as
our analytics data warehouse

00:27:55.010 --> 00:27:57.590
and also the BigTable
and DataStore

00:27:57.590 --> 00:27:59.480
for our in-house
application use,

00:27:59.480 --> 00:28:02.240
which is sitting in the
analyze and explore layer.

00:28:02.240 --> 00:28:04.880
And lastly, we also
enable our DevOps team

00:28:04.880 --> 00:28:07.820
to use Stackdriver's
container registry

00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:12.343
for logging, monitoring,
CI/CD pipeline file platforms.

00:28:16.600 --> 00:28:21.180
So now we all know how
GCP is playing a key role

00:28:21.180 --> 00:28:23.700
in our marketing
platform, enable

00:28:23.700 --> 00:28:27.840
us to surround our guests
for every touchpoint.

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:30.270
But at the same time,
we want to make sure--

00:28:30.270 --> 00:28:34.680
it's important point for us
to apply our infrastructures,

00:28:34.680 --> 00:28:39.060
standards, practices, on top
of GCP for the long term.

00:28:39.060 --> 00:28:42.150
So here's a few key
highlights that we

00:28:42.150 --> 00:28:45.960
set as our GCP foundation.

00:28:45.960 --> 00:28:48.330
For example, backup
recovery strategy.

00:28:48.330 --> 00:28:51.540
We need to make sure that we
have defined the region zones,

00:28:51.540 --> 00:28:53.130
disaster recovery.

00:28:53.130 --> 00:28:55.590
We had the big automation
for scalability.

00:28:55.590 --> 00:28:59.580
We also need to integrate
DevOps, our standard tools

00:28:59.580 --> 00:29:02.820
for monitoring and operations,
governance strategy

00:29:02.820 --> 00:29:07.680
around the technical support,
optimization processes,

00:29:07.680 --> 00:29:12.060
best practices, and also
compute engine and storage

00:29:12.060 --> 00:29:16.410
standards for the OS
patching, licensing, pattern

00:29:16.410 --> 00:29:19.170
for the machine type
and cloud storage.

00:29:19.170 --> 00:29:22.470
And security risk,
also important for us

00:29:22.470 --> 00:29:25.440
to continue to manage the
user roles and groups.

00:29:25.440 --> 00:29:27.203
And then lastly, the networking.

00:29:27.203 --> 00:29:28.620
We need to make
sure that we apply

00:29:28.620 --> 00:29:32.070
the shared VPC clients via
VPN, and DNS, and all of that.

00:29:35.930 --> 00:29:37.114
Thanks, very much.

00:29:37.114 --> 00:29:39.090
